From 5274b5eb4f969e19492873247c1ec455e3ae0254 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Keith Packard <keithp@keithp.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 06:56:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 10/17] test-posix: Check the string functions at guard pages
 and every alignment

Operands that end at, or start at, an inaccessible page, every
alignment of source and destination, lengths 0 to 64 and some larger,
bytes with the high bit set, and overlapping memmove. strnlen, strndup,
strncmp, strncpy, strncat and strlcat get arrays without a null that
end at the guard page; memchr gets lengths past it with the match
before it.
